-- title:
--   Coprime widths make e(s₀) γ(s₀) generate the component group
-- statement:
--   Let $\iota$ be a finite type and let $e \colon \iota \to \mathbb{N}$ be a family of natural numbers (widths) which is pairwise coprime, i.e. $\gcd(e(s), e(t)) = 1$ whenever $s \neq t$, and let $s_0 \in \iota$. Write $X =$ `characterLattice ι` for the submodule of $\iota \to \mathbb{Z}$ cut out as the kernel of `degreeOn ι` $= \sum_{x} \mathrm{proj}_x$, that is, the lattice of integer-valued functions on $\iota$ whose coordinates sum to $0$. Let `gramMap e` be the map $X \to \operatorname{Hom}_{\mathbb{Z}}(X, \mathbb{Z})$ obtained by restricting the bilinear form `widthPairing e` attached to $e$ to $X$ in both arguments, and let `componentGroupProj e` be the quotient map from $\operatorname{Hom}_{\mathbb{Z}}(X, \mathbb{Z})$ onto `componentGroup e` $= \operatorname{Hom}_{\mathbb{Z}}(X, \mathbb{Z}) / \operatorname{range}(\mathrm{gramMap}\ e)$. The assertion is that the cyclic subgroup generated by the class in `componentGroup e` of the functional $(e(s_0) : \mathbb{Z}) \cdot (\mathrm{proj}_{s_0} \circ \iota_X)$, i.e. of $D \mapsto e(s_0) \, D_{s_0}$ on $X$, is all of `componentGroup e`.
--
--   The quotient of $\operatorname{Hom}(X,\mathbb{Z})$ by the image of the Gram map of the width pairing is the combinatorial component group of a two-vertex weighted dual graph, the edges being the crossings with their widths $e(s)$; the statement says that under pairwise coprimality of the widths this group is cyclic, generated by an explicit coordinate functional. It is used by [`ModularCurve.zmultiples_componentGroupProj_smul_coord_eq_top_of_width_eq_jWidth`](thm.html#ModularCurve.zmultiples_componentGroupProj_smul_coord_eq_top_of_width_eq_jWidth), where the widths arising from the resolution of the crossings of the special fibre are seen to satisfy the coprimality hypothesis.
